# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) converts files to
# CRLF on checkout, while `.prettierrc.json` sets `endOfLine: "lf"` — so
# `prettier --check` fails on every file on any Windows machine, including the
# Windows CI runner. `eol=lf` overrides autocrlf for this repository, which is
# what makes the two settings agree.
#
# Nothing here is a shell script or a Windows batch file that would need CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch their bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
